<title>DENMARK: Danish Wise Men see 2.2 percent inflation in 1996.</title>
<headline>Danish Wise Men see 2.2 percent inflation in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The independent Danish Economic Council said in its biannual report on Wednesday that it expected a 2.2 percent rise in consumer prices in 1996 and a 2.6 precent increase in 1997.</p>
<p>In its previous report last May, the council, known as the Wise Men, predicted inflation of 2.4 percent in 1996 and a 2.8 percent rise in 1997.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 969650</p>
</text>
